This src/pscf/cpu directory contains utility functions and classes that 
are analogous to others defined in the src/pscf/cuda directory, but that 
use different hardware: All code defined in this directory is written in
standard C++ and uses standard CPU hardware, whereas analogous code in 
the pscf/cuda directory uses C++/CUDA code to perform some computations 
in parallel on a GPU.  Classes and functions with analogous interfaces 
defined in these two directories are intended to be used interchangeably 
in function templates that are used to create pairs of closely analogous 
executables that use C++ vs CUDA backends.
